<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>Warranties whether express or implied shall be construed as consistent with each other and as cumulative, but if such construction is unreasonable the intention of the parties shall determine which warranty is dominant. In ascertaining that intention the following rules apply:</p><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>Exact or technical specifications displace an inconsistent sample or model or general language of description.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>A sample from an existing bulk displaces inconsistent general language of description.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>Express warranties displaced inconsistent implied warranties other than an implied warranty of fitness for a particular purpose.</p></caml:Content>